## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical familiarity with per-tenant feature flags using Azure App Configuration, a serverless HTTP API, environment scoping with labels, and a basic CI/CD/testing approach.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Functions HTTP trigger and bindings
- Azure App Configuration keys and labels per environment
- Tenant isolation via header; validation
- In-memory caching to reduce App Configuration reads
- Lightweight test strategy: unit tests with mocks, minimal integration tests against a test App Configuration
- GitHub Actions basics: secrets, workflow, and basic tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: fetch per-tenant feature flags
import { AppConfigurationClient } from "@azure/app-configuration";

async function getFeatures(req) {
  const tenant = (req.headers["x-tenant-id"] || "").trim();
  const env = process.env.ENV || "dev";
  const client = new AppConfigurationClient(process.env.APPCONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING);
  const setting = await client.getConfigurationSetting({ key: "featureFlags", label: `${tenant}--${env}` });
  return JSON.parse(setting.value);
}
```

